[Attached document]
CopilotKit Quickstart
Add AI copilots to your React application with CopilotKit. This one-page excerpt covers the three
steps to get a working chat UI in your app.
Install
Add the CopilotKit packages to your project:
 npm install @copilotkit/react-core @copilotkit/react-ui
Provide a runtime
Wrap your application in a CopilotKit provider that points at a runtime endpoint. The provider
coordinates state, tools, and streaming between your React tree and the agent.
 import { CopilotKit } from "@copilotkit/react-core";
export default function App({ children }) {
  return (
    <CopilotKit runtimeUrl="/api/copilotkit">
      {children}
    </CopilotKit>
  );
}
Add a chat UI
Drop the CopilotKit chat component wherever you want the assistant to appear.
 import { CopilotChat } from "@copilotkit/react-ui";
<CopilotChat />
What's next
Read the CopilotKit docs for tools, shared state, human-in-the-loop, generative UI, and the full agent
integration catalog at docs.copilotkit.ai.

